# FROZEN VALIDATION FIXTURE - do not regenerate, do not refresh, do not replace
# with live data.
#
# scripts/reference.py and scripts/validate.mjs both read THIS file, never
# public/data/. That separation is the whole point: public/data/stations.tle is
# rewritten by .github/workflows/update-tle.yml every six hours, and when it was,
# scripts/reference.json silently began comparing the same objects propagated from
# DIFFERENT element sets - ~11,000 km of "deviation" that was not a bug in
# anything. A validation fixture that a cron job can edit is not a fixture.
#
# These are the approximate placeholder elements from the initial commit, at a
# fixed epoch of 2026-09-12T00:00:00Z. They do NOT describe where these objects
# really are, and that does not matter here: the check is whether satellite.js and
# sgp4+skyfield agree on the coordinate and time chain given identical input. SGP4
# does not care whether its elements are real.
#
# If you ever do change this file, scripts/reference.json must be regenerated in
# the same commit:
#     pip install sgp4 skyfield
#     python3 scripts/reference.py > scripts/reference.json
#     npm run validate
